SOAPBOX: Very few FT8 stations were active, and FT4 proved to be the much more effective contest mode. FT8 exchanges are simply too time consuming to sustain a competitive rate. I used N1MM+ with WSJT-X Improved, but the integration between the two is not yet ready for prime time. N1MM still lists PSK as a selectable mode but provides no FT8 or FT4 mode options, requiring me to use PSK with my K3S. In addition, the N1MM/WSJT-X Improved combination disabled the Wait and Pounce and Wait and Call functions in WSJT-X Improved. The software worked, but these limitations made digital contesting more cumbersome than it should be.
